<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">căthē^drārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to an arm-chair</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsellia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					33, 10, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servi,</span>”
				<i>who carry a chair</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>pertaining to the chair</i> or <i>office of a teacher</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">philosophi,</span>”
				<i>teachers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Brev. Vit. 10, 1</span></i>
			; cf. cathedra, II.; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
